## Conversation
User: "Add the new weave agent APIs (github.com/wandb/weave) backed by OTEL to the MCP." First mistaken for the threads API; user corrected: it's the Agents API added recently by Ben Sherman, in the weave repo's `agents` dir. User chose FULL surface (all 8 read endpoints) over a smaller core set, and provided bcanfieldsherman/agents-demo for live verification. Then: "put this up as draft".

## What this adds
8 MCP tools over the Weave Agents observability API (OTel/GenAI agent spans), a data plane SEPARATE from classic Weave calls. New files: weave_api/agents_client.py (AgentsApiClient), mcp_tools/agents.py (tools + descriptions). Registered in server.py and added to _WEAVE_TOOL_NAMES so WANDB_MCP_ENABLE_WEAVE_TOOLS=false disables them too.

## API contract (reverse-engineered; NOT in local weave 0.52.35)
Source of truth: weave/trace_server/agents/types.py @ github.com/wandb/weave (master). Endpoints confirmed via sdks/node/src/generated/traceServerApi.ts + Node SDK request cassettes (sdks/node/src/__tests__/__cassettes__/weaveclient_*.yaml -- these contain real request/response JSON against https://trace.wandb.ai).
Read endpoints (all POST, plain JSON, NOT JSONL-streamed like /calls/stream_query):
  /agents/query                      -> AgentsQueryReq{project_id,filters{agent_name},sort_by[{field,direction}],limit,offset,include_costs} -> {agents,total_count}
  /agents/agent-versions/query       -> {versions,total_count}
  /agents/spans/query                -> AgentSpansQueryReq{project_id,query(Mongo $expr),group_by,measures,sort_by,limit,offset,started_after,started_before,include_details,include_costs} -> {spans|groups,total_count}
  /agents/spans/stats                -> AgentSpanStatsReq{project_id,start,end,granularity,timezone,group_by,metrics[AgentSpanStatsMetricSpec]} -> {columns,rows,...}
  /agents/spans/custom-attrs/schema  -> {attributes,has_more}
  /agents/search                     -> AgentSearchReq{project_id,query,trace_id,conversation_id,agent_name,roles,...} -> {results,total_conversations}
  /agents/traces/chat                -> AgentTraceChatReq{project_id,trace_id,include_feedback} -> AgentTraceChatRes{messages[typed timeline],...}
  /agents/conversations/chat         -> AgentConversationChatReq{project_id,conversation_id,limit,offset,include_feedback} -> {turns:[AgentTraceChatRes],...}
Ingest (write, not exposed): /agents/otel/v1/traces.
Auth: HTTP Basic, base64(":"+api_key) -- same as the calls client. project_id = "entity/project".

## Key design decisions
- Do NOT import weave agent types: pinned weave 0.52.35 predates them; MCP already speaks raw HTTP to the trace server. Request bodies are dicts (None values dropped so server defaults apply); responses returned as dicts.
- AgentsApiClient mirrors WeaveApiClient construction + get_retry_session(); inlines the 3-line basic-auth (matches count_traces.py precedent) rather than abstracting.
- mcp_tools/agents.py: shared _run() envelope = auth check -> track_tool_execution -> AgentsApiError mapping (404 -> agents_api_unavailable, else agents_query_failed) -> _truncate_response -> json.dumps. _truncate_response trims the largest list field to MAX_RESPONSE_TOKENS (reuses TraceProcessor.estimate_tokens) and adds a _truncation note; it does NOT reuse enforce_token_budget (that one is calls/trace-shaped).
- Stats tool: _normalize_stats_metrics turns user-friendly metric inputs into AgentSpanStatsMetricSpec dicts. String "input_tokens" -> {source:field}; derived names (duration_ms,total_tokens,is_error,is_invocation,total_cost_usd,input_cost_usd,output_cost_usd) -> {source:derived}; boolean derived -> aggregations ["count_true"] (sum/avg invalid for boolean per server _ALLOWED_AGGS_BY_TYPE). Full spec dicts pass through.
- query_agent_spans: agent_name shortcut becomes a Mongo $eq on agent_name, AND-combined with any caller query. include_details defaults False to keep payloads lean (raw OTel dumps are huge).

